# .claude/.gitignore — what stays per-developer vs. what gets shared
#
# Everything not listed here is tracked by default (matching endriss's pattern).

# Per-developer Claude Code settings (permissions, allowed tools, model overrides).
# This is the conventional Claude Code location for personal config — never share.
settings.local.json

# Raw session-learning journal — captured by /learnsave before review.
# Curated output (distilled/) and audit trail (archived/) ARE tracked, so the team
# still benefits from /formulate-beliefs once raw notes are reviewed and integrated.
# To share an unsorted learning, run /formulate-beliefs to promote it to distilled/.
.memories/unsorted/*
!.memories/unsorted/.gitkeep

# Anything matching this glob is per-developer scratch (e.g. when experimenting
# with hookify rules locally without committing them yet). Hookify rules meant
# to be shared use the *.local.md naming convention without a leading underscore.
_scratch/
*.scratch.md

# --- Per-machine agent identity. NEVER share. (added 2026-08-18) ---
# bus-config.json declares this agent's identity on the AI bus via session_name,
# which decides BOTH what it stamps on outgoing envelopes AND which inbox it polls.
# Claiming an envelope is a move, not a read — so a copied config makes one agent
# silently consume another's work in the wrong codebase. /Sites/akne declared itself
# "rosacea-galderma-1" from the June 2026 bootstrap until 2026-08-18 for exactly this
# reason. Keep it ignored so the collision can never propagate through git.
bus-config.json

# Compaction checkpoint — per-session, per-worktree by design.
session-state.json

# Local scratch and edit backups
_scratch/
*.scratch.md
*.bak
*.bak-*
